Well of you are right Arnt, although I consider/believe 'consider' and
'believe' be approximate in meaning and intent - any difference is miniscul=
e
compared to the difference between 'God is good' and 'I think God act with
rightfullness and fairness' and so on.

My own "bearing" on lojban as being a language with "naive realism" as
"focus" comes from the fact that predicate logic is its base. E-prime,
regardless if it has such goals explicitly stated or not, hinders dogmatism
by not being the obvius default as it is in english (etc) now. Dogmatism
happens to always be connected to a strong sense of being right, which is a
sort of realistic stance.

Mikael Hall

